@model PlayerDetailViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = $"Player {Model.Code}";
}

@*
    Superseded. GuardianController.Player now renders Views/Shared/FiveCFeedback.cshtml,
    the same 5C page the player sees. Kept as a signpost.

    The "Change consent" button that used to be here linked to Guardian/Consent, which is
    not built. A button that leads to an empty page is a promise the app cannot keep, so it
    says so instead of linking.
*@

<h1>@Model.Code</h1>
<p class="text-muted">@Model.TeamName</p>

<p><strong>Consent:</strong> @ConsentViewModel.Describe(Model.Consent)</p>

<p class="sc-small sc-muted">
    Changing consent is not built yet. It is Brage's, and it goes through
    IConsentService.RecordAsync — the log is append-only.
</p>
